  "question": {
    "text": "Two charges of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mi>μC</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mi>μC</mi></math> are placed at the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> located in an electric field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>20</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The magnitude of the torque acting on the dipole is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo></math>_________."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0063_890f053ab8db.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 93px;\"/></p><p>Given the electric field is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>→</mo></mover></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>20</mn><mo> </mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo> </mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi>cm</mi></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>20</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo> </mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mfrac></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>The formula for calculating the torque is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>τ</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover><mi>p</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>×</mo><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>where,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mover><mi>p</mi><mo>→</mo></mover></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>q</mi><mover><mi>l</mi><mo>→</mo></mover></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>4</mn><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mi>μC</mi><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>Thus, from equation (1), it follows that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>τ</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>×</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>20</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mover><mi>τ</mi><mo>→</mo></mover></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mn>8</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>8</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p>Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
